==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* The M1’s don't have end-lag.
* After [[Sharkman Karate]] got reworked, Water Kung Fu is arguably better for grinding than Sharkman Karate.
* Great for farming, as all moves are AoE and do not have much knockback.
* Fairly good damage, range, and hitbox.
* With enough experience, the player can learn capable combos.
* [[Buddha]] is good with this fighting style, since most abilities do not have any hitboxes.
* All moves damage [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Highly recommended for the [[First Sea]] for its damage, range, and M1.

|'''[Z] Steam-Charged Fist'''
* Decent knockback.
* [[Instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]] on a direct hit.

|'''[X] Deadly Shower'''
* Extremely high range.
* High tick damage.

|'''[C] Heavy Water Punch'''
* Good range.
* Can be used as a travel move, although not very efficient.
** Can dodge attacks in PvP and PvE since it covers a decent range.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Not recommended in PvP because it's quite slow; its upgraded version, [[Sharkman Karate]] is more recommended because of its high combo potential.
* Mainly requires close range. Doesn't in [[Buddha]] transformation.
* Moves require prediction.
* Relatively expensive for [[First Sea]] players since [[Instinct]] is the same amount of [[Money]].

|'''[Z] Steam-Charged Fist'''
* Can be hard to hit in PvP.
* A bit of end lag which, in uncommon but not rare cases, can get the player stuck in the ground.
* Short range.
* Does not deal any damage if used with Transformed Buddha (v2).

|'''[X] Deadly Shower'''
* Requires good aiming skills.

|'''[C] Heavy Water Punch'''
* Can "mess up" and only hit one enemy out of a group.
* Low endlag.
}}
</tabber>

